WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.720 --> 00:00:07.680
18. Is it a fair trade?

2
00:00:07.680 --> 00:00:12.880
You may have noticed a fair trade label on a product you bought recently. More and more

3
00:00:12.880 --> 00:00:18.000
companies are joining the fair trade movement and showing it on their packaging. But what

4
00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:24.560
exactly is fair trade? Fair trade is a social movement designed to create better trading

5
00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:30.920
conditions for farmers, artists, and other producers in developing countries. Fair trade

6
00:00:30.920 --> 00:00:36.720
businesses also promote sustainable farming and production methods. They see trade between

7
00:00:36.720 --> 00:00:42.640
developing and developed nations as a way to help solve problems like poverty. To do

8
00:00:42.640 --> 00:00:48.360
this, they follow different, more compassionate principles than most other businesses. Fair

9
00:00:48.360 --> 00:00:54.400
trade businesses pay more than current market prices for goods. They believe the low prices

10
00:00:54.400 --> 00:01:01.000
most buyers pay are unfair to sellers. Higher prices allow the producers selling goods to

11
00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:08.120
earn more, invest more, and expand their businesses if they want to. In addition, fair trade companies

12
00:01:08.120 --> 00:01:14.240
try to avoid working with middlemen. They connect sellers directly with their buyers.

13
00:01:14.240 --> 00:01:19.400
This means that sellers don't have to pay a third person to help them reach a market.

14
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:25.240
Many fair trade businesses also use and promote environmentally friendly practices. They may

15
00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:30.200
provide credit to sellers who want to grow their businesses. And of course, fair trade

16
00:01:30.200 --> 00:01:36.760
means that no slave or child labor can be used at any point. Of course, fair trade has

17
00:01:36.760 --> 00:01:42.760
a few problems of its own. Research shows the poorest fair trade sellers aren't earning

18
00:01:42.760 --> 00:01:48.560
any more money now than they did before. It's also hard to make sure that fair trade practices

19
00:01:48.560 --> 00:01:55.560
are actually being followed and sometimes people cheat. So is fair trade really fair? For now,

20
00:01:55.560 --> 00:01:58.800
it seems the consumer doesn't have a final answer.
